1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,400
<i>Previously, on Night Shift...</i>

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,100
Maya, you're late again.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,900
Traffic was a nightmare.
Don't start, Hale.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,800
I'm not starting anything,
I'm just saying the captain

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,000
has been asking for you all morning.

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,300
Fine. Let's cut to the chase.

7
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,900
What did the witness tell you?

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,600
She finally spilled the beans
about the warehouse.

9
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,000
And?

10
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,500
The shipment comes in Friday night,
around midnight, give or take.

11
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,300
That's a piece of cake.

12
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,400
Nothing about this case
has been a piece of cake, Maya.

13
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,000
- Coffee?
- God, yes.

14
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,700
You look like you haven't slept
since Tuesday.

15
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,200
I was going to...

16
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,800
...call you last night, but
my phone died.

17
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,500
Sure it did.

18
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,400
[phone buzzing]

19
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,100
Detective Hale.

20
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,200
Yes, sir. We're on our way.

21
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,900
The captain wants us downtown.
Now.

22
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,300
Break a leg in there.

23
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,800
You're coming with me,
whether you like it or not.

24
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,600
Fine, but I'm driving.
Your driving is a crime scene.

25
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,300
♪ Soft jazz playing ♪

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,400
Captain Reyes, you wanted to see us?

27
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,800
Sit down, both of you.
We have a problem.

28
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,500
Someone inside this department
has been tipping off

29
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,200
the Kessler crew.

30
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,000
A mole?

31
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,300
Every raid we've planned this year
has come up empty.

32
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:27,900
That's not bad luck,
that's a pattern.

33
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:30,600
So what do you want us to do,
sir?

34
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,900
Keep Friday's operation
between the three of us.

35
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:36,000
Not a word to anyone.

36
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,100
Understood.

37
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,700
And Maya? Don't be late.

38
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,900
Not this time.

39
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:47,200
<i>Friday. 11:52 p.m.
Pier 9.</i>

40
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,800
Here we go. Showtime.
